WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.550
Fire Tornado Double Drive!

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.990
The winner of this year's Holy Road is...

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.160
Yes, the famous Raimon Jr. High you're all familiar with!

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.450
Hello, I'm the announcer, Tominaga Jun.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:31.240
Today, we will present to you a special program to commemorate Raimon's Holy Road championship.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:39.490
We'll cover all the secrets to Raimon Eleven's strength that led the team to the championship!

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.870
We're really on TV.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.650
I'm so excited!

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.600
Crap, it already started!

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.770
Did they show us already?

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:49.830
It just began.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.980
Don't worry, we've got it recording.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.730
That was a close call.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:43.320
Our editors narrowed down the secrets to Raimon's strength to three points.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:49.610
Without further ado, let's see what secrets guided them to the championship!

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.970
The secrets to Raimon Eleven's strength, #1.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:55.210
The riverbank is the holy land of hard work!

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.150
<i>Why, you!</i>

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:21.070
Raimon's zephyr-like charge passionately, passionately shook the spirits of all soccer youths around the nation!

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:25.450
I'm sure many of you remember their famous matches.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.410
I've become quite a fan of Raimon's soccer myself!

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.490
<i>Let's win this!</i>

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.160
<i>Come out! My Avatar, Instrumentalist Maestro!</i>

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.410
Especially Shindou-kun!

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.440
He's so cool!

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.460
His disciplined yet mysteriously charming manner is so irresistible!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.380
She understands!

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:50.520
I'm now at the riverbank, where many soccer youths have gathered.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.840
Let's interview them for a bit.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.600
Everyone, do you like the Raimon Eleven?

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.400
We love them!

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.060
Then which Raimon Eleven do you like specifically?

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:03.980
Tenma!

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.310
His Avatar is so cool!

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.630
Tsurugi-kun!

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.550
Amagi-san!

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.530
Shindou, isn't he cool?

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.880
It's gotta be Kirino-kun!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.030
If you're a man, it's Sangoku-san!

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.040
Shinsuke-kun! He's so cute!

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.160
She called you cute, Shinsuke.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.620
Great, great!

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.730
You've all got fans now.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.640
This is kind of embarrassing.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.120
No one said my name.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:41.140
Actually, this riverbank is a very important place for the Raimon Eleven.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:47.200
After all, many of their hissatsu techniques were created here!

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.670
At the final stage of Holy Road,

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:53.700
Matsukaze Tenma-kun took up the position as the team's captain despite being only a first-year.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.710
It seems he always practices here.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.910
His first hissatsu technique, Soyokaze Step, was also created here.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.360
<i>I'll do it!{8}</i>

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.190
<i>I'll  </i>become<i> real soccer!</i>

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.630
<i>Soyokaze Step!</i>

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:14.010
<i>Wind?</i>

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.940
<i>I got past Captain...</i>

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.810
<i>All right! That endless practice finally paid off!</i>

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:30.070
Nishizono Shinsuke-kun, another first-year, also created his first hissatsu technique, Full Throttle Jump, here!

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.740
<i>Full Throttle Jump!</i>

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:50.970
And Fire Tornado Double Drive, which spurred the counterattack in the finals...

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:54.440
...is yet another result of the practice done at the riverbank!

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.880
<i>It's such a hard technique to pull off.{41}</i>

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:04.460
<i>Keep going!</i>

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.110
<i>Tsurugi...</i>

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:10.280
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:18.390
This is also the place where Coach Endou brought the team together not long after his arrival.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.680
So many different things happened here.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:26.540
<i>For starters, show me your kick strength.{7}</i>

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.340
<i>One shoot each.</i>

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.800
<i>Death Sword!</i>

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:03.210
<i>What?</i>

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:14.600
All starting with Tenma-kun, this riverbank is full of memories for the Raimon Eleven.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.890
Riverbank! Thank you!

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:23.480
Please be there to support Raimon's hard work from now on, too!

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.630
The secrets to Raimon Eleven's strength, #2.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.030
The goddesses who support the players!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:35.990
<i>But the goddess of victory will never smile upon those who don't actively seek to win.</i>

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:39.560
That was a quote from Coach Endou.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.240
The goddess of victory.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:47.420
Our editors found that one of the secrets to Raimon Eleven's strength is the goddesses that support them.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.000
First up are the managers of Raimon's soccer club.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.010
This makes me kind of nervous.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.050
I wonder how they'll introduce us.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.890
Get off!

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:01.470
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.350
<i>Soccer?</i>

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:08.100
<i>Could it be...?</i>

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.320
<i>You guys are serious downers!{8}</i>

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.570
<i>Is there no "OMG I love soccer!" like the first-years in you?</i>

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.900
<i>Nope.</i>

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.470
<i>Hayami!</i>

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.180
<i>Midori-chan, no violence.</i>

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:25.820
The second-years, Seto Midori-san and Yamana Akane-san.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.120
And first-year Sorano Aoi-san.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.180
These three who helped Tenma-kun and the others during practice and continued cheering them on...

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.220
...could very well be considered the secret actors leading to the championship.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:38.880
<i>Did I surprise you?</i>

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:39.720
<i>Sorry about that.</i>

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.890
The counselor, Otonashi Haruna-sensei.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:49.430
As a manager ten years ago, she is a witness to Raimon's history such as Raimon's first championship,

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:55.000
as well as Inazuma Japan's first championship.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.200
<i>You must be Matsukaze Tenma-kun.{18}</i>

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:05.180
Next is Coach Endou's wife, Endou Natsumi-san.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:10.710
She has supported Coach Endou with all of her wonderful cooking.{iyaiya}

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.800
<i>Welcome back, Tenma.{3}</i>

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.650
<i>Go ahead!</i>

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.140
<i>Thanks for the food!</i>

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.840
<i>Stop asking that every day!</i>

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:28.000
And you can't forget the landlord of the Kogarashi Manor, where Tenma-kun lives.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.130
Kino Aki-san!

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:35.960
Always watching over Tenma, she would sometimes act as a parent and talk to Tenma about soccer.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:42.110
I can't believe I'd be here with you celebrating Raimon's championship again, Otonashi-san.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.910
I've always dreamed it would happen.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.790
I wonder if I can be like Otonashi-sensei and the others when I grow up?

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:58.490
We might end up supporting the Raimon Eleven just like them ten years from now.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.880
That sounds pretty amazing!

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:05.340
Maybe I'll be the coach then!

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.320
No way.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.400
Can you do things firmly like Coach Endou?

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.700
I can!

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.810
Tenma, you're the goalkeeper!

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.610
That's nothing like him!

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:19.400
We love soccer!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:23.970
We love soccer!

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:30.180
The secrets to Raimon Eleven's strength, #3.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.960
Raimon spirit!

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:36.000
<i>I guess you could call it Raimon spirit.{31}</i>

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.080
Here's what you've been waiting for!

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.970
The secrets to Raimon Eleven's strength, #3.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.450
Raimon spirit!

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:50.130
As a famous school known throughout the nation, this is the source of Raimon's strength.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.770
All of you probably know that the alumni of Raimon's soccer club...

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:59.220
...are now actively playing soccer in Japan and around the world.

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.420
<i>So this must be fate as well.{14}</i>

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:04.700
<i>Shindou!</i>

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.740
<i>It's been forever since I last saw you, Japan.{30}</i>

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:18.490
Endou Mamoru, previously the captain who brought fame to the school,

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:21.010
had been playing for a professional team overseas,

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:26.260
but he is currently back at his home school to lead the team as the coach.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.230
<i>With your own hands, get the #1 title in Japan!</i>

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.480
<i>Make one in with a boom!</i>

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.770
<i>With your spirited shoots!</i>

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:43.650
After the Holy Road prelims, Kidou Yuuto, another Raimon alumni who worked as Raimon's trainer,

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.890
came to fill in for Coach Endou while he took a leave.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:51.500
Coach Kidou was previously Teikoku Academy's commander.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:57.070
After Holy Road, he has returned to the role of being Teikoku Academy's commander.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.370
<i>Endou.{24}</i>

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:00.420
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:03.260
<i>Their desire to win is making both teams strike each other at full force.</i>

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.680
This <i>is soccer!</i>

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.730
By inheriting the Raimon spirit from their predecessors, including Coach Endou and Coach Kidou,

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:15.840
these 16 members who make up the Raimon Eleven have won the Holy Road championship!

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:21.490
The Raimon Eleven's hissatsu technique index!

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.740
Fence Of Gaia!

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:34.940
Dash Train!

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:47.050
Atlantis Wall!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.130
Surfing Pierrot!

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:02.760
Zeroyon!

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:11.780
Sidewinder!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.490
The Mist!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.340
Bushin Renzan!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.340
War God Multi-Slash

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.690
Hunter's Net!

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:48.740
Extend Zone!

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.620
Britannia Cross!

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:58.750
Among these players, the following four have played a huge role.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:03.170
First is the captain, Matsukaze Tenma-kun.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:09.670
As the successor to Raimon spirit, he never gave up as he pulled everyone along with his wind.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.640
Mach Wind!

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:21.850
<i>All right, I'll be the captain.{40}</i>

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:26.070
<i>If I have my mind set to do it, I'll do it no matter what!</i>

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:36.230
<i>Reach the heavens!</i>

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.790
<i>This is...</i>

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:42.120
<i>Demon God Pegasus Arc!</i>

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:45.440
<i>Even I...</i>

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:52.370
Next is the team's playmaker, Shindou Takuto-kun.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:56.680
His great leadership brings the team together.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.710
<i>Instrumentalist Maestro!</i>

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.440
<i>You can do it. I know you can.{40}</i>

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:10.980
<i>Tenma!</i>

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.900
<i>Harmonics!</i>

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.500
<i>Is that all you've got?</i>

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.470
And the ace striker, Tsurugi Kyousuke-kun.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:37.840
With his dangerous charm, he caused quite a storm within the team.

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.390
<i>Let me play in the match.{17}</i>

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.230
Death Drop!

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.950
Lost Angel!

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:07.490
Last but not least, with his small body but BIG fighting spirit, Nishizono Shinsuke-kun!

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:10.110
He's a hard worker who has even brought out an Avatar!

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.370
<i>Rage Jump Defense!{46}</i>

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.120
<i>Go!</i>

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.640
<i>Kaboom!</i>

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.890
<i>An Avatar came out...{37}</i>

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:27.150
<i>Majin The Hand!</i>

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:37.280
You can feel the Raimon spirit even stronger with hissatsu tactics.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:44.390
They're passionate plays that can only happen when everyone's feelings are together.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:48.000
We'll show you Raimon's hissatsu tactics all at once!

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:50.590
<i>Tenma!</i>

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.150
<i>Tenma!</i>

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.920
Shin-sama, you're so noble and amazing!

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.060
<i>Hayami!</i>

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:01.640
Tsurugi really helped us out for this one.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.420
<i>Ultimate Thunder!</i>

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.730
<i>Take this!</i>

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:10.940
<i>Kageyama!</i>

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:11.600
<i>Okay!</i>

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.200
<i>Hissatsu tactics!</i>

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.910
<i>Double Wing!</i>

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.410
You did a great job there, Kageyama.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.050
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:33.960
<i>Hissatsu tactics! Flying Route Pass!</i>

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:37.840
<i>Kirino!</i>

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:43.260
Those pitch-downs were just way too much.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:46.180
I even fell into the water.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:53.770
Then let's have an interview with the captain, Matsukaze Tenma-kun, about Raimon spirit.

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:57.810
Tenma-kun, congratulations on the championship.

00:18:57.810 --> 00:19:00.740
Th-Th-Thank you very much!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.750
Whoa, you're so nervous!

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.220
Of course I was!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.200
It was my first time for something like that.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:13.940
What do you personally think the secret to Raimon's victory is?

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:18.420
I-I think it's teamwork.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:23.260
No matter what kind of plays you make, you can't get anything done if the other members aren't working together.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.550
I see.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:30.760
We were really a mess a first, so I didn't know how it'd work out at first.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:36.780
But everyone really loves soccer, so I just kept thinking it'd work out somehow.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.570
You're a little <i>too</i>  nervous there.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:45.120
It's turning into a nonsense ramble.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.530
I guess so...

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:50.830
Now Tenma-kun, do you have something to say for your fans?

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.600
Yes, um...

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.670
Please continue cheering on Raimon.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:59.540
We'll work hard to be Japan's number one next year, too!

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:03.300
You sound way too much like an honor student.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.060
I couldn't help it!

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.310
I was just really nervous, okay?

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.670
Tenma-kun, thank you.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:13.850
Next time, we'll look into the source of Raimon spirit even further.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:18.050
The spotlight will be on the time when Coach Endou was a member of the soccer club.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:22.720
We'll look into the secret of their strength even deeper!

00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:26.320
We'll see you again tomorrow at this time!

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.690
Huh? It's over?

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.140
Yeah.

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.250
It's over.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:37.090
They didn't use my interview!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:40.720
They didn't even interview me in the first place!

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.170
That's because you went off somewhere.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:48.720
We really won the championship because so many people were there to cheer us on.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.340
<i>You're a bit like him.</i>

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.590
<i>When I look at you, I end up remembering someone I knew a long time ago.</i>

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.680
<i>Matsukaze Tenma.</i>

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:58.420
<i>Yes, sir?</i>

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.570
<i>Put on one of the spare uniforms.</i>

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:03.690
<i>I'm testing you.</i>

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:08.370
<i>That's why what's important here, Tenma, is you.{11}</i>

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.670
<i>I'm sorry for my team's rudeness.</i>

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:15.250
<i>It's really unfortunate. I wanted to play a real game with you.</i>

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:17.530
<i>So you're Kyousuke's teammate?{15}</i>

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:18.530
<i>Yes.</i>

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:19.750
<i>I hope you're getting along with him.</i>

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:22.960
<i>That passion you had... That's what real soccer is.{18}</i>

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.410
<i>They're the Akizora Challengers.{21}</i>

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.720
